FIRMWARE - Mytek Digital Stereo192-DSD DAC using the USB2 interface

This repository does not distribute the proprietary Mytek firmware blobs.

The driver expects three files at runtime:

- mytekl2.ihx
- mytekcf.bin
- mytekap.ihx

They must be obtained by the device owner from a lawful Mytek firmware/driver
package and installed locally under:

  /lib/firmware/mytek/

For the private, tested setup used by the current maintainer, the supported
files from Mytek USB2 driver package 1.35.22 have these SHA256 values:

  76e05f7f7602997a0de9e0371201349f1904f6d75f1ffe920367fd329a14c041  mytekap.ihx
  4e2158606cffa41e24657e97a526e26b218b0334cc2c76465389d5b6e2013127  mytekcf.bin
  ab09812dba64002bd220626febf58501adc3b00f5e3b8e76c46f083357e68d35  mytekl2.ihx

The files are intentionally excluded by .gitignore and must not be committed to
this repository or attached to public releases.

Historical note
---------------

The original project documented extracting equivalent firmware files from the
Mytek Windows driver and copying them to /lib/firmware/mytek. Older supported
firmware revisions and their historical SHA1 values remain available in the
repository history.

Current validated firmware loading behavior
-------------------------------------------

The maintained driver branch fixes a re-probe bug that previously prevented the
multi-stage firmware sequence from continuing automatically after USB
re-enumeration. On the validated Volumio 4.119 / Raspberry Pi setup, a cold DAC
power-on proceeds through the firmware stages automatically and reaches:

  Mytek USB firmware 3.1.35 loaded.

Known hardware/firmware limitation:

If the Raspberry Pi is rebooted while an already initialized Mytek remains
powered on, the device can appear as pre-initialized but with missing FPGA
firmware and fail to register. In that state, power-cycle the Mytek DAC; a Pi
reboot or manual module reload is not required.
